{"id":"~Jan_Kautz1","name":"Jan Kautz","counts":{"accepted_papers":2,"first_position_papers":0,"co_first_author_papers":null,"corresponding_author_papers":null,"Oral":2},"papers":[{"id":"Bshs9HDDiu","title":"World Action Models are Zero-shot Policies","abstract":"State-of-the-art Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models excel at semantic generalization but struggle to generalize to unseen physical motions in novel environments. We introduce DreamZero, a World Action Model (WAM) built upon a pretrained video diffusion backbone. Unlike VLAs, WAMs learn physical dynamics by predicting future world states and actions, using video as a dense representation of how the world evolves. By jointly modeling video and action, DreamZero learns diverse skills effectively from heterogeneous robot data without relying on repetitive demonstrations. This results in over 2x improvement in generalization to new tasks in new environments compared to state-of-the-art VLAs in real-robot experiments. Crucially, through model and system optimizations, we enable a 14B autoregressive video diffusion model to perform real-time closed-loop control at 7Hz.","summary":"以联合预测未来视频与动作的 World Action Model 学习物理先验。DreamZero 研究多样化数据下的零样本任务泛化、跨构型视频迁移，以及新机器人上的少量数据适应。","type":"Oral","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","模仿与示范学习","生成策略与扩散","安全、泛化与鲁棒性"],"title_topics":[],"authors":["~Seonghyeon_Ye1","~Yunhao_Ge1","~Kaiyuan_Zheng1","~Shenyuan_Gao1","~Sihyun_Yu2","~George_Kurian1","~Suneel_Indupuru1","~You_Liang_Tan1","~Chuning_Zhu1","~Jiannan_Xiang1","~Ayaan_Naveed_Malik1","~Kyungmin_Lee1","~William_Liang1","~Nadun_Ranawaka_Arachchige1","~Jiasheng_Gu1","~Yinzhen_Xu1","~Guanzhi_Wang1","~Fengyuan_Hu2","~Avnish_Narayan1","~Johan_Bjorck2","~Jing_Wang79","~Gwanghyun_Kim1","~Dantong_Niu1","~Ruijie_Zheng1","~Yuqi_Xie1","~Jimmy_Wu1","~Qi_Wang58","~Ryan_Julian2","~Danfei_Xu1","~Yilun_Du1","~Yevgen_Chebotar1","~Scott_Reed1","~Jan_Kautz1","~Yuke_Zhu1","~Linxi_Fan2","~Joel_Jang1"],"institutions":["NVIDIA"],"pdf":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.15922","openreview":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=Bshs9HDDiu","project":["https://dreamzero0.github.io"],"code":["https://github.com/dreamzero0/dreamzero"],"poster_date":"2026-11-09","poster_time":"5:00–6:30 PM","poster_venue":"JW Marriott","poster_number":51,"hardware":[{"model":"Agibot G1","env":["real"],"reviewed":false}],"has_social_sample":true,"role_evidence":{"cofirst":[],"corresponding":[],"project_lead":["Seonghyeon Ye","Yuke Zhu","Linxi Fan","Joel Jang"],"page":1,"note":"† Project Leads；* Core Contributors，均不等同共同一作或通讯。"},"author_role":{"id":"Bshs9HDDiu","position":33,"first":false,"roles":[]}},{"id":"2dEfANeQL7","title":"GRAIL: Generating Humanoid Loco-Manipulation from 3D Assets and Video Priors","abstract":"Scaling humanoid loco-manipulation requires robot-compatible demonstrations across diverse objects, whole-body motions, and scene geometries, but teleoperation and motion capture are difficult to scale because each collection depends on physical setups, instrumented actors, and robot operation. We present GRAIL, a digital generation pipeline that remains fully virtual until deployment: it composes 3D assets, simulator-ready scenes, and priors from video foundation models (VFMs) to synthesize interactions without rebuilding physical environments or teleoperating the robot. Rather than reconstructing unconstrained in-the-wild videos, GRAIL starts from fully specified 3D configurations in which object geometry, camera parameters, metric scale, environment depth, and a robot-proportioned character are known before video generation and reused during reconstruction. This privileged setup better conditions 4D recovery, allowing model-based object tracking, human motion estimation, and interaction-aware optimization to reconstruct metric 4D human-object interaction (HOI) trajectories with reduced depth ambiguity and morphology mismatch. We retarget the recovered motions to a humanoid robot and train complementary task-general trackers: an object-aware latent adaptor for manipulation and a scene-aware tracker for terrain traversal. GRAIL produces over 20,000 sequences spanning pick-up, object manipulation, sitting, and terrain traversal. Using only GRAIL-generated data, we train egocentric visual policies through a sim-to-real pipeline and deploy them on a Unitree G1 humanoid, achieving 84% real-world success on diverse object pick-up and 90% success on stair-climbing. Code and data will be publicly released.","summary":null,"type":"Oral","topics":["视觉语言动作与基础模型","模仿与示范学习","世界模型与仿真","移动、全身与人形","空间几何与三维"],"title_topics":["移动、全身与人形","空间几何与三维"],"authors":["~Tianyi_Xie1","~Haotian_Zhang7","~Jinhyung_Park1","~Zi_Wang6","~Bowen_Wen1","~Jiefeng_Li1","~Xueting_Li2","~Qingwei_Ben1","~Haoyang_Weng1","~Yufei_Ye1","~David_Minor1","~Tingwu_Wang1","~Chenfanfu_Jiang3","~Sanja_Fidler1","~Jan_Kautz1","~Linxi_Fan2","~Yuke_Zhu1","~Zhengyi_Luo1","~Umar_Iqbal3","~Ye_Yuan5"],"institutions":["NVIDIA","University of California, Los Angeles"],"pdf":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.05160","openreview":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=2dEfANeQL7","project":["https://research.nvidia.com/labs/dair/grail","https://research.nvidia.com/labs/dair/publication/xie2026grail"],"code":[],"poster_date":"2026-11-10","poster_time":"5:00–6:30 PM","poster_venue":"JW Marriott","poster_number":216,"hardware":[{"model":"Unitree G1","env":["real"],"reviewed":false},{"model":"OAK 相机","env":["real"],"reviewed":true}],"has_social_sample":true,"role_evidence":null,"author_role":{"id":"2dEfANeQL7","position":15,"first":false,"roles":[]}}],"topics":{"视觉语言动作与基础模型":2,"模仿与示范学习":2,"生成策略与扩散":1,"安全、泛化与鲁棒性":1,"世界模型与仿真":1,"移动、全身与人形":1,"空间几何与三维":1},"role_counts":{},"role_papers_reviewed":1,"profile":null,"portfolio":null,"needs_identifier_review":false,"affiliation_evidence":{"direct":[{"institution":"NVIDIA","method":"single_byline_institution","author_excerpt":"Chebotar Scott Reed Jan Kautz Yuke Zhu Linxi Jim Fan Joel J","institution_excerpt":"Fan Joel Jang NVIDIA Project Leads *C